<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>PresenceSync</displayName>
  <description>Policies for PresenceSync (sync Teams presence across tenants)</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="PresenceSync">PresenceSync</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_PresenceSync_0_1">PresenceSync 1.0 and later</string>
      <string id="ClientId">Set the app registration client ID</string>
      <string id="ClientId_Help">Sets the client ID (application ID) of the app registration PresenceSync signs in with.

Enabled: the specified client ID is used. Users cannot change it in the settings unless the policy "Allow custom client ID" is enabled.

Disabled or not configured: users enter the client ID themselves.

Format: GUID, e.g. 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000. Invalid values are ignored and logged.

Registry: Software\Policies\PresenceSync, value ClientId (REG_SZ). Computer policy takes precedence over user policy.</string>
      <string id="AllowCustomClientId">Allow custom client ID</string>
      <string id="AllowCustomClientId_Help">Enabled: a client ID set by policy is only a default for an empty setting; users may enter a different client ID.

Disabled or not configured: a client ID set by policy is mandatory and locked.

Registry: Software\Policies\PresenceSync, value AllowCustomClientId (REG_DWORD, 1/0).</string>
      <string id="HomeTenantId">Set the home tenant</string>
      <string id="HomeTenantId_Help">Sets the organization's home tenant (tenant ID as GUID).

Enabled: PresenceSync adds the home tenant automatically at startup and marks it as home. Users cannot remove it. If the Windows account is a member account of this tenant, PresenceSync signs in without user interaction; otherwise the user clicks "Sign in" once.

Disabled or not configured: users add the home tenant themselves.

Registry: Software\Policies\PresenceSync, value HomeTenantId (REG_SZ).</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="ClientId">
        <textBox refId="ClientId">
          <label>Client ID:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="HomeTenantId">
        <textBox refId="HomeTenantId">
          <label>Tenant ID:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
